															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser deleted" data-id="3927912"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/common--images/avatars/default/a16.png" alt=""/>(account deleted)</span> <span class="odate time_1535323880 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Aug 2018 22:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3930589">
									

<p>I tell ya, there must be something in the water&#8230;a draft I'm working on features the words &quot;lithosphere&quot; &quot;asthenosphere&quot; and &quot;tectonic&quot;, cross-references black-boxed SCPs, and <em>was</em> targeting the 4997 slot. (Begrudgingly, I believe I'll have to find another SCP slot.)</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A couple of split hairs:</p>
<p>The black-boxing in the article I just don't get. There's a lot of it and I'm not sure why. The number of limbs the creature has is the prime example; why does that need to be redacted? Am I missing something? If it is all just for mystery, I don't think it has an effect as strong as a real numbers would.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Additional theories claim it may be photosynthetic</p>
</blockquote>
<p>A Foundation scientist thinks a subterranean creature that hasn't surfaced for 2 million years might be photosynthetic?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4997 is <em>coming off</em> of a dormant period</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I think the clinical tone wavers here.</p>
<p>I think the Note from Dr. P█████ makes him seem kinda like a doofus. &quot;magnitude, pun intended&#8230;&quot;, it's exactly what a goofball would <em>write down</em>. I mean that is okay if that's what you're going for.</p>
<p>I'm not so sure about the Level 5 collapsible. Seems anticlimactic and that it isn't really all that hush; could be included in the description where the initiative to neutralize the anomaly is mentioned. Seems odd that the O5 would be using the article as essentially a mailbox too.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>There's room for some improvement, but the original pictures, “asthenobiology,” the technical competence of the work, and the first sentence of the third paragraph got you the +1.</p>

							</div>

								
					
